rockchip: phy: snps-pcie3: increase SRAM init timeout to 20000us

The RK3568 PCIe3 PHY SRAM init poll in rockchip_p3phy_rk3568_init uses a
500us timeout, which can occasionally time out during startup, causing
intermittent PCIe enumeration failure. Rockchip upstream confirmed 500us
is too tight and recommends 20000us (fix not yet in 6.12 mainline, so
this is a backport/port).

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-snps-pcie3.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-snps-pcie3.c
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
 	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(priv->phy_grf,
 				       GRF_PCIE30PHY_STATUS0,
 				       reg, SRAM_INIT_DONE(reg),
-				       0, 500);
+				       0, 20000);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(&priv->phy->dev, "%s: lock failed 0x%x, check input refclk and power supply\n",
 		       __func__, reg);
